  "description": "UtcMilliTime for .NET 8.0 + .NET 10+ provides Unix time milliseconds (Int64) timestamps, similar to JavaScript's Date.now(), with cross-platform support and NTP synchronization. Features Task-based async APIs, async Main support, and conversion extensions (ToIso8601String, ToUtcDateTime, etc.).\n\nUsage:\nusing UtcMilliTime;\nITime time = Clock.Time;\ntime.SuppressNetworkCalls = false; // Enable NTP sync\nvar timestamp = time.Now; // Int64 timestamp\nstring iso = timestamp.ToIso8601String(); // ISO-8601 string\n\nFor async Main:\nawait Clock.CreateAsync();\n\nSee https://github.com/JPKusumi/UtcMilliTime for details.",
